#### Uncertainty Assignment

The uncertainties due to the mismatches shown in section 5.6.1 are calculated by producing corrected spectra with an offset applied to the corrections. For the distance of closest approach of the V0 to the primary vertex cut, in order to determine the scale of the uncertainty, corrected spectra are produced with a 0.8 cm cut on the raw yields, and a 0.7 cm cut on the corrections. The 0.1 cm difference (0.8-0.7) represents an upper limit on the difference in the mean of each distribution (raw vs. Monte Carlo) shown in figure 5.17. As the mismatch leads to the corrected yields being too low when the cut of 0.8 cm is applied to both the raw yields and corrections, the offset gives a larger corrected yield as the applied corrections are smaller, and therefore represents the scale of the uncertainty. For the TPC hit cut, the offset chosen is 2 (again upper limit on the difference in the respective means) which gives

